  "where_to_look": "a view whose declared axis is shortened by the resolver is a defect this repository has already had once: runtime/sim/memory.py's loop-bound axis test shortened DeepSeek-V4.1's compressor gather from a 2-row key/value pair to ONE row, because a loop term's stride happened to match a block of some axis, and the fix was to require that the axis can hold one whole iteration (``dim[axis] >= step``). The shape here is the same -- a declared extent of ten resolving to one -- on the index score's output rather than on a gather's."
